#. ~ Description of terrain "white grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of grass covered in white latex-based paint, with neat lines "
"designed for recreational sports."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf green"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass mowed very short and neat."
msgstr "Une zone d'herbe verte ayant été coupée très courte et régulièrement."

#. ~ Description of terrain "grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of hardy grass about ankle high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "long bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long bamboo shoots about shin high."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de longues pousses de bambou arrivant un peu en dessous du genou."

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, brown, dead bamboo shoots covered in white fungus."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "long grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, shaggy grass about shin high."
msgstr ""
"Une zone d'herbes longues et broussailleuses arrivant un peu en dessous du "
"genou."

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of tall grass about head high."
msgstr "Une zone d'herbes hautes arrivant à hauteur de tête."

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  Many shoots are just "
"barely pushing above the ground."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de jeunes pousses de bambou arrivant au niveau de la cheville, la "
"plupart émergeant juste du sol."

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  The smallest shoots have "
"already been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de jeunes pousses de bambou arrivant au niveau de la cheville. Les "
"plus petites pousses ont déjà été récoltées."

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely "
"planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even "
"displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which "
"are quite unlike olives, but this particular plant has been harvested "
"already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely "
"planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even "
"displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which "
"are quite unlike olives."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers "
"with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly "
"sweet berries in autumn, if it hadn't been picked clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers "
"with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly "
"sweet berries in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Drooping black berries adorn the shrub during autumn.  These have a "
"distinctive star-shaped fold and look quite juicy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Drooping black berries adorned this shrub, but the shrub was picked clean."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the "
"settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-"
"like fruits, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the "
"settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-"
"like fruits."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could "
"probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'une de quelques espèces différentes du genre \"Prunus\" "
"présentes en Nouvelle Angleterre, ayant pour fruits des cerises durant "
"l'été. Si vous examiniez ses branches de plus près, vous pourriez "
"probablement en trouver quelques grappes mûres."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'une de quelques espèces différentes du genre \"Prunus\" "
"présentes en Nouvelle Angleterre, ayant pour fruits des cerises durant "
"l'été. On dirait que toutes les cerises mûres on déjà été cueillies."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could "
"probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'une de quelques espèces différentes du genre \"Prunus\" "
"présentes en Nouvelle Angleterre, ayant pour fruits des pêches durant l'été. "
"Si vous examiniez ses branches de plus près, vous pourriez probablement en "
"trouver quelques unes bien mûres."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'une de quelques espèces différentes du genre \"Prunus\" "
"présentes en Nouvelle Angleterre, ayant pour fruits des pêches durant l'été. "
"On dirait que toutes les pêches mûres on déjà été cueillies."

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries "
"grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries "
"grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "magnolia tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Part of an ancient lineage of broadleaf trees known for their large white "
"flowers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Patchy grass which has withered and died."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "woodchips"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small splinters of wood laid out in a layer to prevent unwanted plants from "
"growing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and its edible young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and you might be able to eat its young leaves in the spring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this pine tree have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive being warped like this."
msgstr ""
"Les branches de cet arbre ont été altérées jusqu'à ce qu'elle ressemblent "
"une forme qui rappellent les triangles de Sierpinski, l'arbre n'ayant pas "
"survécu cette transformation traumatique."

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr ""
"Ce qui reste d'un grand arbre caduque appartenant au genre Carya. Rien ne "
"peut être récolté de ce pauvre arbre mort à part du bois si vous souhaitez "
"l'abattre."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  "
"It gets its name from its sweet sap, which can be tapped with a spile and "
"used to make syrup."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  "
"This one's tapped with a spile."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr ""
"Les branches de cet arbre à feuilles caduques ont été transformée en "
"spirales, ce processus l'ayant apparemment tué."

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Un \"Pyrus communis\" ou poirier commun, produisant ses fruits durant "
"l'automne. Si vous examiniez ses branches de plus près, vous pourriez "
"probablement en trouver plusieurs assez mûres."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Un \"Pyrus communis\" ou poirier commun, produisant ses fruits durant "
"l'automne. On dirait que toutes les poires mûres ont déjà été cueillies."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a "
"pine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a "
"pine.  Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and "
"many of the cones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could "
"be harvestable again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark "
"blue berries in autumn, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark "
"blue berries in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""
"Cet arbre est un membre du genre \"Malus\", produisant le fruit connu sous "
"le nom de pomme. Si vous examiniez ses branches durant l'automne vous "
"pourriez probablement trouver en trouver quelques unes bien mûres."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr ""
"Un membre du genre \"Malus\", cet arbre produit des fruits communément "
"connus sous le nom de pommes. Il n'y a pas l'air d'avoir de pommes mûres "
"dessus en ce moment."

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, "
"its fruits are small and sour.  If you examined the branches more closely, "
"you could probably find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, "
"its fruits are small and sour.  There do not appear to be any ripe "
"crabapples now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Cet arbre est un membre du genre \"Sambucus\", et produit des baies "
"communément connues comme baies de sureau durant l'été."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr ""
"Cet arbre est un membre du genre \"Sambucus\", et produit des baies "
"communément connues comme baies de sureau durant l'été. Il n'y a pas l'air "
"d'avoir de baies mûres en ce moment."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  In the winter and spring, the sap rich roots can be harvested to "
"make a sweet beverage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  This tree's roots have been harvested, any more and the tree "
"will die."
msgstr ""

