#. ~ Description of "soviet tanker helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A Soviet era tanker helmet.  Its distinctive foam pads are meant to protect "
"a tank driver from bumps against the cramped interior."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "helmet liner"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A cloth liner worn inside a helmet to help keep your head warm in cold "
"climates.  It might also provide some padding against helmets that didn't "
"have any."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "conical helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A conical iron helm with additional protection for the neck, associated with "
"the Mongol Empire."
msgstr ""
"Un casque conique en fer avec protection supplémentaire pour la nuque, "
"associé à l'empire mongol."

#. ~ Description of "firefighter helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A distinctive helmet worn by firefighters to protect from falling debris.  "
"More than just a piece of firefighting equipment, it serves as a badge of "
"honor and respect."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "baseball helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic helmet that covers the head and ears, designed to protect "
"against a baseball to the head."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "army helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A heavy helmet that provides excellent protection from all sorts of damage.  "
"It is labeled as an advanced combat helmet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "football helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A heavy polycarbonate helmet normally worn by football players.  It comes "
"with a visor to protect the eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un casque lourd en polycarbonate normalement porté par les joueurs de "
"football américain. Une visière y est attachée pour protéger les yeux."

#. ~ Description of "biosilicified chitin helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet crafted from the carefully cleaned and pruned biosilicified "
"exoskeletons of acidic ants.  Acid-resistant but brittle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "riding helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet designed to protect from falls and kicks involving horses, has a "
"small peak to protect from glare."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "jockey skull cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid "A helmet designed to protect from falls and kicks involving horses."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "kettle helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet fashioned in the shape of a cap with a wide brim.  It leaves the "
"face and neck exposed, but offers a bit of cover from glare and rain."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pot helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet made from a soup pot.  It's not very good protection, but it's "
"better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Un casque fait maison fait avec un pot de soupe. Ce n'est pas une très bonne "
"protection, mais c'est mieux que rien."

#. ~ Description of "chitin helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet made from the exoskeletons of insects.  Covers the entire head; "
"very light and durable."
msgstr ""
"Ce casque a été fabriqué à partir d'exosquelettes d'insectes. Il protège "
"toute la tête, est très léger et durable."

#. ~ Description of "leather helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid "A helmet made of shaped and hardened leather."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "full-face motorcycle helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet that covers the entire head along with glareproof visors, offering "
"the best protection for when you ride around on your motorcycle.  Activate "
"to raise the visor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "full-face motorcycle helmet (raised visor)"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet that covers the entire head along with glareproof visors, offering "
"the best protection when you ride around on your motorcycle.  The visor is "
"raised.  Activate to put down the visor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sheet metal helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A helmet that looks like a crude bucket with the face cut out.  It comes "
"with a bevor to distribute some of the weight to your shoulders, as well as "
"cloth padding to keep your bell from being rung."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pot helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid "A huge makeshift helmet made from a canning pot."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tactical helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight black helmet that provides excellent protection from all sorts "
"of damage.  It has a military rail system for attachments."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "airsoft helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight helmet that is fashioned to look like a real military helmet, "
"but is made of plastic and only protects against BB's and other light "
"threats.  It has a military rail system for attachments."
msgstr ""
"Un casque conçu pour imiter un véritable casque militaire, mais fait en "
"plastique et peu utile pour vous protéger contre quoi que ce soit de plus "
"qu'un plomb. Son effort d'imitation à un côté positif dû au rail présent sur "
"le casque auquel vous pouvez attacher des objets."

#. ~ Description of "kabuto"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A medieval Japanese helmet with a scowling face mask that provides excellent "
"protection to the entire head and face."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "visored plate helm (raised)"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A medieval helmet made of steel platemail.  It provides excellent coverage "
"for the head and neck, though at the moment not the face.  Activate it to "
"lower the visor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "visored plate helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A medieval helmet made of steel platemail.  It provides excellent coverage "
"for the head and neck.  Activate it to raise the visor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "barbute helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A medieval helmet that provides excellent protection for the head, with a Y "
"shaped opening for the face."
msgstr ""
"Un casque médiéval fournissant une excellente protection pour la tête, avec "
"une ouverture en Y pour le visage."

#. ~ Description of "great helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A medieval helmet that provides excellent protection to the entire head, at "
"the cost of great encumbrance."
msgstr ""
"Un casque médiéval qui offre une excellente protection à toute la tête au "
"prix d'un encombrant très important."

#. ~ Description of "flak helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A simple helmet meant to protect the head from fragmentation and impacts.  "
"Its simple steel construction renders it outdated by modern military "
"standards."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid "A solid, single piece closed bronze helmet with a slit for the eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un heaume complet et fermé consistant d'une seule pièce de bronze et ayant "
"une fente pour les yeux."

#. ~ Description of "pickelhaube"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A spiked helmet once worn by German military officers.  The spike is "
"ornamental."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "turban helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"A style of helmet once used in the Middle East, cylindrical on the top with "
"protection for the nose and ears but nothing lower."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bike helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid "A thick foam helmet.  Designed to protect against concussion."
msgstr ""
"Un épais casque en mousse, conçu pour protéger contre les commotions "
"cérébrales."

#. ~ Description of "skid lid"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"Also called a crash helmet, this piece of headgear is often worn by bikers "
"and extreme sportsmen who prefer to keep their faces uncovered."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "galea"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"An Imperial Roman helmet, with distinct projections protecting the sides of "
"the head."
msgstr ""
"Casque de la Rome Impériale avec des saillies protégeant les cotés de la "
"tête."

#. ~ Description of "tactical full helmet"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"An all-encompassing black helmet that covers your entire face and neck, "
"providing excellent protection from all sorts of damage."
msgstr ""
"Un casque intégral noir qui protège le visage et la nuque et qui procure une "
"excellente protection."

#. ~ Description of "Corinthian helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"An ancient Greek bronze helmet that provides excellent protection for the "
"head, with slits for the eyes and mouth."
msgstr ""
"Ancien casque Grec en bronze qui fourni une excellente protection de la "
"tête, avec des fentes pour les yeux et la bouche."

#. ~ Description of "nasal helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"An early medieval helmet with a projection guarding the nose, to better "
"protect the face without obstructing vision.  Proper Viking gear, unlike the "
"stereotypical horned helm."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pot great helm"
#: data/json/items/armor/helmets.json
msgid ""
"An enclosed helmet made from a stock pot with a blanket stuffed inside to "
"cushion it.  There are strings tied to the handles to help fasten it to your "
"body, but it's hot and unwieldy."
msgstr ""

