msgid_plural "books of fairy tales"
msgstr[0] "livre de contes de fées"
msgstr[1] "livres de contes de fées"
msgstr[2] "livres de contes de fées"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/book/young.json
msgid "children's book"
msgid_plural "children's books"
msgstr[0] "livre pour enfants"
msgstr[1] "livres pour enfants"
msgstr[2] "livres pour enfants"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/book/young.json
msgid "coming of age novel"
msgid_plural "coming of age novels"
msgstr[0] "roman d'apprentissage"
msgstr[1] "romans d'apprentissage"
msgstr[2] "romans d'apprentissage"

#. ~ Description of "slaked lime"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
" A handful of slaked lime, a white odorless powder with many uses.  Also "
"known as calcium hydroxide."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "improvised rocket fuel"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder-and-sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of sulfur"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A chunk of pure sulfur.  Break it up to use it."
msgstr "Un morceau de souffre pur. Brisez le pour pouvoir l'utiliser."

#. ~ Description of "rhodonite"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of rhodonite.  It has manganese dioxide covering and going through "
"it in veins, which can be obtained using a chisel."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plutonium"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of unshielded plutonium.  You should probably get very far away from "
"this, if you enjoy not being irradiated."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de plutonium sans aucune protection. Vous devriez probablement "
"rester très loin de ceci si vous ne voulez pas être irradié(e)."

#. ~ Description of "rosin"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A chunk of yellowish rosin, usable as a flux for soldering."
msgstr "Un morceau de colophane jaunâtre, utilisable comme fondant de soudure."

#. ~ Description of "zincite"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of zincite.  Could be refined into zinc oxide, then into zinc by "
"reduction with a source of carbon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "acetic anhydride"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless liquid that smells strongly of vinegar.  If you have enough "
"chemical knowledge, you could use it to easily convert morphine into heroin."
msgstr ""
"Un liquide incolore ayant un arome de vinaigre fort. Avec assez de savoir en "
"chimie, vous pourriez l'utiliser pour fabriquer de l'héroïne à partir de "
"morphine."

#. ~ Description of "benzene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless, highly flammable liquid with a sweet odor, one of the "
"elementary petrochemicals.  Being used primarily as a precursor to the "
"manufacture of chemicals with more complex structure, it's a major "
"industrial chemical, but finds limited use in consumer items because of its "
"toxicity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "toluene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless, toxic, and highly flammable liquid which smells like paint "
"thinner.  It's predominantly used as an industrial feedstock and a solvent, "
"and is also used as an intoxicative inhalant in a manner unintended by "
"manufacturers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "concentrated paralytic"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A concentrated paralytic agent, originally from a triffid.  Given your "
"experience with its effects (chiefly gathered while sourcing this batch) and "
"their striking similarity to earthly flora, you figure it's related to "
"curarines.  Might come in handy in crafting more useful things."
msgstr ""
"Un agent paralytique concentrée extrait d'un organisme triffide. Au vu de "
"votre expérience de ses effets (principalement acquise en récupérant cet "
"échantillon) et sa ressemblance troublante avec la flore terrestre, vous "
"supposez que ceci est une molécule ou un mix de molécules proche des curares "
"et pourrez être utile durant la synthèse ou la fabrication de différentes "
"choses."

#. ~ Description of "acetylene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A flammable gas that explodes under pressure.  Combined with oxygen, "
"acetylene makes a great welding gas."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bee venom gland"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of "
"honeybee venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with "
"the right know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un organisme fragile et légèrement frémissant pour la production et le "
"stockage du venin d'abeille. Vous pourriez en extraire des produits "
"chimiques très utiles avec le bon savoir-faire, mais seulement si vous vous "
"dépêchez."

#. ~ Description of "wasp venom gland"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of wasp "
"venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with the right "
"know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un organisme fragile et légèrement frémissant pour la production et le "
"stockage du venin de guêpe. Vous pourriez en extraire des produits chimiques "
"très utiles avec le bon savoir-faire, mais seulement si vous vous dépêchez."

#. ~ Description of "sac of paralytic venom"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A grayish, flexible vesicle filled to the brim with the potent paralytic "
"agent the triffids use to subdue still-moving fertilizer such as yourself.  "
"If you know your way around poisons you might be able to find a use for it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sand"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of New England sand.  If you had a stoked furnace, you could turn "
"it into glass.  Otherwise, it's only good for making cement."
msgstr ""
"Du sable. Avec un four alimenté vous pourriez en faire du verre. Sinon ce "
"n'est bon qu'a en faire du ciment."

#. ~ Description of "wood ashes"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of almost-weightless residue left after the burning of some "
"substance."
msgstr "Le résidu presque sans poids laissé par la combustion d'un objet."

#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate pellets"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate pellets.  These pellets are commonly used as a "
"component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved in water "
"to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this quality in "
"this new world?"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de granules de nitrate d'ammonium. Communément utilisé dans la "
"fabrication d'engrais et d'explosifs. Vous pouvez aussi dissoudre ces "
"granules dans de l'eau pour en diminuer nettement la température, mais est-"
"ce ceci très utile dans ce nouveau monde?"

#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate.  This white, crystalline powder is commonly "
"used as a component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved "
"in water to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this "
"quality in this new world?"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de nitrate d'ammonium. Cette poudre blanche cristalline est "
"couramment utilisée dans les fertilisants et les explosifs. On peut aussi la "
"dissoudre dans l'eau pour en diminuer nettement la température, mais est-ce "
"utile dans ce nouveau monde?"

#. ~ Description of "black gunpowder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, a mix of saltpeter, charcoal, and sulfur.  "
"Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot produced when it "
"burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used to make some "
"vicious bombs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "ANFO"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of brownish pellets, made by allowing ammonium nitrate to absorb "
"an organic fuel.  This ammonium nitrate/fuel oil mixture, or ANFO, is a "
"common industrial explosive due to its stability and low price.  Burns fast, "
"but needs an explosive primer to detonate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbide, giving off a faint, garlic-like smell.  "
"Commercially, calcium carbide was used for on-the-spot manufacture of "
"acetylene and historically to power acetylene lamps.  If mixed with water "
"and sealed, it will explode with little strength, but with a relatively loud "
"noise that might be useful as a distraction."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de carbure de calcium sentant légèrement l'ail. Utilisé pour "
"fabriquer de l'acétylène et alimenter les lampes à acétylène. Peut être "
"utilisé pour causer une petite explosion assez bruyante pouvant détourner "
"l'attention si mélangé avec de l'eau dans un récipient fermé."

#. ~ Description of "calcium carbonate"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbonate powder, typically derived from lime or "
"shells.  Useful for a number of roles, such as sugar production, fracking, "
"construction, paint additives and antacid medicine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chromium oxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of chromium oxide.  This substance, typically known as the only "
"stable green pigment for paints, is also a mild oxidizer, which can be mixed "
"with aluminum powder to make thermite for welding.  If one had access to a "
"CVD machine and a laboratory worth of reagents, they might be able to "
"produce very durable ceramic layers."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'oxyde de chrome. Cette substance, connue comme le seul pigment "
"vert pour les peintures, et également utilisée comme comburant, qui mélangée "
"avec de la poudre d'aluminium peut produire de la thermite pour la soudure. "
"Celui qui a accès à un laboratoire avec les composants nécessaires pourrait "
"produire de la céramique très résistante."

#. ~ Description of "ferric chloride"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of dark green crystalline powder, with a weak pungent smell "
"similar to that of hydrochloric acid.  Commonly used as a Lewis acid for "
"catalyzing various chemical reactions."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre crystalline vert foncé possédant une faible odeur "
"désagréable similaire à celle de l'acide hydrochlorique. Communément utilisé "
"come acide Lewis pour catalyser des réactions chimiques variées."

#. ~ Description of "aluminum powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of finely-ground aluminum powder.  This strong reducing agent was "
"used in combination with various oxidants for chemical welding and "
"explosives alike.  Just before the Cataclysm, however, it was the basis of "
"virtually all commercial metallic-hued paints and anti-corrosive coatings."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre fine d'aluminium. Ce fort agent réducteur était "
"utilisé avec divers oxydants pour la soudure chimique et les explosifs. "
"Juste avant le cataclysme, il servait dans les peintures métalliques et les "
"revêtements anti-corrosion."

#. ~ Description of "soap flakes"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of flakes shaved off a bar of soap, suitable for use in a washing "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de copeaux issus d'une barre de savon utilisables pour lancer "
"une machine à laver."

#. ~ Description of "chestnuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a chestnut tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de noix dures issues d'un marronnier, toujours dans leurs "
"coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "hazelnuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a hazelnut tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de noix dures issues d'un noisetier, toujours dans leurs "
"coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "hickory nuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a hickory tree, still in their shells."
msgstr "Une poignée de noix de caryer, encore dans leurs cosses."

#. ~ Description of "peanuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a peanut bush, still in their shells."
msgstr "Une poignée de cacahuètes toujours dans leurs coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "pecans"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a pecan tree, still in their shells."
msgstr "Une poignée de noix de pécan toujours dans leurs coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "pistachios"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a pistachio tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de noix dures issues d'un pistachier, toujours dans leurs "
"coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "walnuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a walnut tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de noix dures issues d'un noyer, toujours dans leurs coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "almonds"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from an almond tree, still in their shells."
msgstr "Une poignée d'amandes toujours dans leur coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "acrylamide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of highly carcinogenic white powder that can be readily "
"polymerized into a whole bunch of useful water-soluble gels."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre blanche hautement cancérigène facilement polymérisée "
"pour former une variété de gels utiles solubles dans l'eau."

#. ~ Description of "butternut husks"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of husks from a butternuts, emptied of their meat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "manganese dioxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of manganese dioxide powder.  Occurring naturally in the mineral "
"pyrolusite, it is used commercially in the production of alkaline and zinc-"
"carbon batteries."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre de dioxyde de manganèse. Se trouvant naturellement "
"dans le minerai de pyrolusite, elle est utilisée dans la production "
"commerciale des piles alcalines et des piles zinc-carbone."

#. ~ Description of "butternuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of nuts from a butternut tree, still in their shell."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de noix douces issues d'un noyer cendré toujours dans leurs "
"coquilles."

#. ~ Description of "potassium chloride"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium chloride.  Although it occurs naturally in the "
"mineral sylvite, it can be produced as a byproduct of the reaction of "
"saltpeter and hydrochloric acid.  It can be used for making fertilizer, or "
"potassium hydroxide by way of electrolysis."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de chlorure de potassium. Bien que trouvable naturellement dans "
"la sylvine minérale, il peut être produit artificiellement par la réaction "
"du salpêtre et de l'acide chlorhydrique. Il peut est utilisé pour faire des "
"engrais, ou de l’hydroxyde de potassium par électrolyse."

#. ~ Description of "potassium hydroxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium hydroxide.  Commonly called caustic potash, it was "
"mainly used industrially for its caustic nature.  It can be used as an "
"electrolyte in alkaline batteries, among other applications."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'hydroxyde de potassium. Communément appelé potasse caustique, "
"il était principalement utilisé industriellement pour sa nature caustique. "
"Il peut être utilisé comme électrolyte dans des piles alcalines, parmi "
"d'autres utilisations."

#. ~ Description of "sulfur"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of pure sulfur.  Primarily used to make battery acid, sulfur is "
"sometimes used as fuel for explosives.  Can be burned to produce acidic "
"smoke that is deadly to bacteria and humans alike, or oxidized to make paper-"
"bleaching agents.  It also serves as a basis for many kinds of fungicide."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de soufre pur. Principalement utilisé pour fabriquer de l'acide "
"de batterie, le soufre est également utilisé en tant que carburant pour "
"explosifs ou ingrédient pour une solution fongicide. Il est aussi possible "
"de le brûler pour relâcher des vapeurs toxiques fatales pour tout animal, "
"plante et bactérie y étant exposé(e)."

#. ~ Description of "iodine crystals"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of resublimed crystals of the element iodine, they can be used as "
"an antiseptic, but are also used in the making of methamphetamine."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de cristaux d'iode resublimés pouvant être utilisés durant la "
"fabrication d'antiseptiques, mais aussi durant la synthèse de métamphétamine."

#. ~ Description of "rock salt"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of rock salt crystals.  Could be refined into table salt."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de sels gemme. Il pourrait être transformé en sel de table."

#. ~ Description of "saltpeter"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of saltpeter.  Sometimes used as a fertilizer, this ubiquitous "
"nitrate is the principal constituent of black gunpowder and simple rocket "
"propellants, such as rocket candy."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de salpêtre. Parfois utilisé comme fertilisant, ce nitrate "
"omniprésent est le composant principal de la poudre à canon et des "
"combustibles de simple fusées tel que le rocket candy."

#. ~ Description of "shredded rubber"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of shredded rubber, usable as a mulch now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "thermite"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un mélande d'aluminium et d'oxyde de fer. Il brûle à des températures "
"extrêmes, et s'utilisait pour les soudures. C'est une très bonne matière "
"incendiaire."

#. ~ Description of "nickel powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-white metallic powder composed of nickel.  Common "
"industrial uses include production of stainless steel as well as other "
"alloys."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre métallique blanc argenté composé de nickel. "
"Communément utilisé en industrie pour fabriquer de l'acier inoxydable ainsi "
"que d'autres alliages."

#. ~ Description of "limestone"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of small chunks of limestone.  Useful for experiments at science "
"fairs, but pretty useless as ammo.  Maybe something could be crafted from "
"this stuff…"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de morceaux de calcaire. Utile pour des expériences "
"scientifiques, mais pas pour en faire des munitions. On peut peut-être en "
"faire quelque chose..."

#. ~ Description of "antimony trichloride"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of soft, colorless powder with a sharp pungent odor, also known as "
"butter of antimony.  It's a catalyst for polymerization, hydrocracking, and "
"chlorination reactions, and has some other niche uses."
msgstr ""
"Une poudre molle et incolore à l'odeur âcre, autrement connue sous le nom de "
"beurre d'antimoine. C'est un catalyseur pour les réactions de "
"polymérisation, d'hydrocraquage et de chloration, ainsi que d'autres "
"utilisations plus niches."

#. ~ Description of "hexamine"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of waxy hexamine tablets which could be broken up into smaller "
"crumbs if needed.  This ubiquitous fuel was used to start up almost every "
"garden grill, and no 'real' camping trip could do its cooking without it, "
"until the Cataclysm.  Nowadays, it is even more valuable than before, being "
"the key component in the preparation of several military-grade explosives."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de tablettes cireuses d'hexamine capable d'être cassées en plus "
"petits morceaux si nécessaire. Ce carburant omniprésent était utilisé pour "
"démarrer a peut prêt n'importe quel barbecue et aucune 'véritable' sortie "
"camping ne pouvais avoir lieu sans. Ceci est maintenant encore plus précieux "
"pour votre survie, d'autant plus qu'il est possible de préparer de nombreux "
"explosifs de qualité militaire ayant l'hexamine pour élément clé."

#. ~ Description of "zinc oxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of zinc oxide.  It can be reduced into zinc, or used for some "
"other reactions of its own."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'oxyde de zinc. Elle peut être réduite en zinc, ou utilisée "
"pour d'autres réactions qui lui sont propre."

#. ~ Description of "zinc powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of zinc powder.  While commercially used mostly in cosmetics and "
"for paints, hobbyists used to mix it with sulfur to make basic rocket fuel "
"or a smokescreen.  When treated with a strong acid, it will produce hydrogen."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre de zinc. Commercialement utilisée pour la cosmétique "
"et les peintures, les amateurs l'utilisait avec du soufre pour en faire du "
"combustible à roquette ou des écrans de fumée. Si on le traite avec un acide "
"fort, il produit de l'hydrogène."

#. ~ Description of "niter"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A large crystal of niter, the mineral form of potassium nitrate.  It can be "
"processed into saltpeter."
msgstr ""
"Un grand cristal de nitre, forme minérale du nitrate de potassium.  il peut "
"être raffiné en salpêtre."

#. ~ Description of "potassium lye"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A liquid form of potassium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with "
"care."
msgstr ""
"Une solution liquide d'hydroxide de potassium. Hautement corrosive, à "
"manipuler avec précaution."

#. ~ Description of "lye"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with care."
msgstr ""
"Une solution liquide d'hydroxide de sodium. Hautement corrosive, à manipuler "
"avec précaution."

#. ~ Description of "latex"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A liquid precursor to rubber found in some plants."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "citric acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A manufactured form of citric acid that is commonly used as an additive in "
"food, cleaning agents, and nutritional supplements."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "gravel"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A marble-sized bit of stone."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel grille"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A metal grille.  It can be used as a framework for making a chemical "
"catalyst."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fermented fertilizer liquid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A mixture of fermented biomass, will become liquid fertilizer after simple "
"treatment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fermentable fish mixture"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A mixture of fish, sugars, and water.  Wait about two months for them to be "
"fermented in an open tank."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fermentable liquid mixture"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A mixture of various organic wastes and water.  Wait about two months for "
"them to be fermented in a tank.  Also, biogas production will start after "
"one month."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "acidic electrolyte paste"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A moisturized mixture of zinc chloride and manganese dioxide, slightly "
"acidic.  It can be used in the production of zinc-carbon batteries."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange légèrement acidique de chloride de zinc et de dioxide de "
"manganèse ayant été humidifié. Utilisé pour produire des piles zinc-carbone."

#. ~ Description of "liquid fertilizer"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A nutrient-rich elixir for plants."
msgstr "Un liquide riche en nutriments conçu pour nourrir des plantes."

#. ~ Description of "cobalt-60 pellet"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A piece of unshielded radioactive material that used to be a part of some "
"nuclear industry equipment.  You have yet to find some use for it, and you "
"probably shouldn't stand near it."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de matière radioactive non protégée qui faisait autrefois partie "
"de certains équipements de l'industrie nucléaire. Vous n'avez pas encore "
"trouvé d'utilité pour lui et vous ne devriez probablement pas vous en "
"approcher."

#. ~ Description of "soil"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A pile of loosely-packed, slightly damp loamy soil.  This mixture of sand, "
"silt and clay is ideal for growing plants."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de terreaux argileux légèrement humide. Ce mélange de sable, de limon "
"et d'argile est idéal pour la croissance des plantes."

#. ~ Description of "fertility supplement"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A pill for those looking to have children.  It is of no use to you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "detergent"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder."
msgstr "Une poudre de lavage populaire avant le Cataclysme."

#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide premix"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A powdered mixture of coke and lime ready to be smelted into usable calcium "
"carbide in an arc furnace."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange en poudre de charbon et de chaux prêt à être fondu en carbure de "
"calcium dans un four à arc."

#. ~ Description of "peptone water powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A pre-mixed salty solution of protein and sugar meant for bacteria to eat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hickory root"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A root from a hickory tree.  It has an earthy smell."
msgstr "Un racine de caryer. Il à une senteur terreuse."

#. ~ Description of "limestone shard"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A small shard of limestone.  Pretty flimsy and not much of a weapon, but its "
"alkaline properties may yet find some use."
msgstr ""
"Un petit éclat de calcaire. Fragile et peu fiable en tant qu'arme, mes ses "
"propriétés alcalines pourraient être utiles."

#. ~ Description of "nanomaterial canister"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A steel canister containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper, and other "
"elements in specifically engineered atomic-scale configurations.  A "
"nanofabricator can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pine resin"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A sticky, sludgy mass of sap harvested from a pine tree."
msgstr "Une masse de résine de conifère épaisse et collante."

#. ~ Description of "silicone caulk"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A thick gray paste used as a sealant in many construction projects."
msgstr ""
"Une pâte grise épaisse utilisée pour étanchéifier ayant de nombreuses "
"utilisations."

#. ~ Description of "concentrated venom"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A transparent, lightly greenish liquid, refined from the venom of bees and "
"wasps.  Active ingredients include (nor-)adrenaline, dopamine, histamine, "
"and protein toxins.  It is now relatively stable, but will require further "
"separation to be useful for anything other than killing you."
msgstr ""
"Un liquide transparent, légèrement verdâtre, obtenu en raffinant du venin "
"d'abeille ou guêpe ayant pour ingrédients actifs (nor-)adrénaline, dopamine, "
"histamine et plusieurs protéines toxiques. Rendu plus ou moins stable pour "
"l'instant, mais plus vous allez avoir besoin d'isoler certaines substances "
"pour fabriquer quelque chose à partir de ceci qui soit bon pour quoi que ce "
"soit d'autre qu'être un poison virulent."

#. ~ Description of "sac of triffid fungicide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A triffid sac filled with what appears to be a triffid-produced antifungal "
"agent.  It will likely already work as an antifungal compound for more "
"offensive applications, but requires further refining before it can be used "
"as a medical drug."
msgstr ""
"Une poche de liquide antifongique ayant été produit par un organisme "
"triffide. Vous pourriez l'utiliser tel quel comme produit antifongique "
"offensif, mais vous allez devoir le raffiner un peu plus avant qu'il soit "
"raisonnable de l'utiliser comme médicament antifongique."

#. ~ Description of "phenol"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A useful and potent solvent with a wide range of reactive applications.  It "
"can be used to make a huge number of plastics and polymers, it can be an "
"antiseptic, it can strip paint and break down epoxy, and it can burn your "
"skin away like tissue paper under a heat gun.  Wear gloves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "ether"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A useful industrial solvent, and the first inhalative anesthetic in "
"widespread use.  Its uncomfortable side effects and tendency to explode "
"caused it to fall out of favor decades ago in the developed world.  If you "
"can't get the good stuff, however, it might make a passable substitute."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "anesthetic"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A variety of powerful hypnotic, analgesic, and stimulative drugs.  It's "
"intended for use in specialized medical equipment, and can't be administered "
"manually.  You can reload an anesthesia kit with it."
msgstr ""
"Une variété de puissantes drogues hypnotiques, analgésiques et stimulantes. "
"Elle est conditionnée pour être utilisée avec un équipement médical "
"spécialisé, et ne peut être administrée manuellement. Vous pouvez recharger "
"un kit d’anesthésiant avec cela."

#. ~ Description of "wooden bead"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A wooden bead.  It can be used to craft inscribable jewelry or create a "
"beaded curtain door."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "ANFO"
msgstr[1] "ANFO"
msgstr[2] "ANFO"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "APEX"
msgid_plural "APEX"
msgstr[0] "APEX"
msgstr[1] "APEX"
msgstr[2] "APEX"

#. ~ Description of "APEX"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Acetone peroxide: this fine, white crystalline powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, with a fruit-like smell when pure."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "acetone"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Acetone, best known as the primary constituent of most nail polish "
"removers.  Flammable, and can be easily used for potent homemade explosives, "
"as demonstrated by the terrorist attacks of 2016."
msgstr ""
"De l'acétone, principalement connue pour ses propriétés de décapant. "
"Inflammable, elle peut facilement servir pour faire des explosifs, comme "
"l'ont démontré des attaques terroristes en 2016."

#. ~ Description of "fungicide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Agricultural-grade chemical anti-fungal powder designed to destroy "
"infections in plants."
msgstr ""
"Un agent chimique anti-fongique conçu éradiquer les infections fongiques "
"végétales."

#. ~ Description of "insecticide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Agricultural-grade chemical insecticide powder designed to eradicate insect "
"pests."
msgstr ""
"Un agent chimique insecticide conçu pour éradiquer les insectes nuisibles."

#. ~ Description of "glycerol"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Also called glycerin, this clear, odorless liquid is both a handy skin "
"moisturizer and an ingredient necessary to make dynamite."
msgstr ""
"Également appelé glycérine, ce liquide clair et inodore est à la fois un "
"hydratant pour la peau pratique et un ingrédient nécessaire à la fabrication "
"de la dynamite."

#. ~ Description of "ammonia solution"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Ammonium hydroxide, a common household cleaning agent."
msgstr "De l'hydroxyde d'ammonium, souvent utilisé comme produit de nettoyage."

#. ~ Description of "white phosphorous"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  Extremely flammable, produces "
"toxic smoke, you can use it to make smoke bombs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "small portion of red phosphorous"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  It's what you use to light "
"matches, but can also be used in the synthesis of methamphetamine.  You "
"could use it to make bombs, and if you were truly desperate you might even "
"be able to use it as a propellant for bullets."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "red phosphorous"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  It's what you use to light "
"matches, but can also be used in the synthesis of methamphetamine.  You "
"could use it to make bombs, and if you were truly desperate you might even "
"be able to use it in small portions as a propellant for bullets."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "liquid ammonia"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Anhydrous ammonia, a useful chemical compound.  It must be stored under "
"pressure or refrigerated.  Don't even think about drinking it."
msgstr ""
"De l'ammoniaque anhydre, un produit chimique utile. Doit être stocké sous "
"pression ou réfrigéré. Ne pensez même-pas à essayer de boire ceci."

#. ~ Description of "toxic acidic blood"
#. ~ Description of "virulent acidic blood"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Blood mixed with acidic compounds, extremely corrosive, a means of refining "
"this could net some useful chemicals."
msgstr ""
"Du sang ayant été mixé avec de puissants acides extrêmement corrosifs. Vous "
"pourriez probablement isoler des produits chimiques utiles en le distillant."

#. ~ Description of "foul acidic blood"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Blood mixed with acidic compounds, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, a "
"means of refining this could net some useful chemicals."
msgstr ""
"Du sang ayant été mixé avec de puissants acides et dégageant une odeur "
"nauséabonde. Vous pourriez probablement isoler des produits chimiques utiles "
"en le distillant."

#. ~ Description of "putrid acidic blood"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Blood mixed with acidic compounds, smells putrid, a means of refining this "
"could net some useful chemicals."
msgstr ""
"Du sang ayant été mixé avec de puissants acides et dégageant une odeur "
"putride. Vous pourriez probablement isoler des produits chimiques utiles en "
"le distillant."

#. ~ Description of "agar"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Clear flakes of processed seaweed that can be dissolved in boiling water to "
"create a very sturdy, temperature-resistant gel.  Not only is it good for "
"making gels to separate molecules by size, but it's a great cheat ingredient "
"to make sure your jellies set properly."
msgstr ""
"Flocons transparents d'algues transformées qui peuvent être dissous dans de "
"l'eau bouillante pour créer un gel très solide et résistant à la "
"température. Non seulement c'est bon pour fabriquer des gels pour séparer "
"les molécules par taille, mais c'est un excellent ingrédient de triche pour "
"garantir que vos gelées prennent correctement."

#. ~ Description of "formic acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Common in nature as an insect venom, this substance has a number of "
"industrial uses such as preservation and manufacturing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "composition B"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Composition B is an explosive consisting of castable mixtures of RDX and "
"TNT.  It is used as the main explosive filling in artillery projectiles, "
"rockets, land mines, hand grenades, and various other munitions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "acetic acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and "
"antifungal agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several "
"types of perfumes, but would making perfume not be too fancy for post-"
"apocalyptic New England?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Concentrated hydrogen peroxide is a powerful oxidant, violently decomposing "
"in contact with most reducing agents.  Can be used as rocket fuel or to make "
"high explosives.  Causes severe burns to any organic matter and may ignite "
"it on contact."
msgstr ""
"De l'eau oxygénée concentrée. Peut s'utiliser pour fabriquer du combustible "
"à roquettes ou des explosifs. Provoque de sérieuses brûlures sur les "
"matières organiques et peut même les enflammer au contact."

#. ~ Description of "dimethyl sulfoxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It has the unusual property "
"of being absorbed very quickly through the skin, causing a garlic flavor in "
"the mouth, even if it touched your arm."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chloroform"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Famous for its properties as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
"very good solvent.  In particular, it's used a lot in nuclear magnetic "
"resonance spectroscopy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "formaldehyde"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Formaldehyde, here dissolved in water, was widely used before the Cataclysm "
"as a precursor to production of many chemicals and materials and as an "
"embalming agent.  Easily identifiable by its pungent odor.  Terribly toxic, "
"carcinogenic, and volatile."
msgstr ""
"Formaldéhyde, ici dissout dans l'eau, était largement utilisé avant le "
"Cataclysme comme précurseur à la production de nombreux produits chimiques "
"et matériaux ainsi que comme agent d'embaumement. Facilement identifiable à "
"son odeur âcre. Terriblement toxique, cancérigène et volatile."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"
msgstr[2] "HMTD"

#. ~ Description of "HMTD"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long."
msgstr ""
"Peroxyde d'hexamine : cette fine poudre jaunâtre est un explosif primaire "
"puissant utilisé pour amorcer la détonation d'explosifs plus stables comme "
"le RDX. Relativement stable mais mieux vaut ne pas le stocker trop longtemps."

#. ~ Description of "sewage"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Horrible sludge from the sewers with an awful stench."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hydrochloric acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Hydrochloric acid, also known as muriatic acid.  It is a strong acid that "
"has a distinctive smell, important and frequently used ever since its "
"discovery.  It still has a vast multitude of uses."
msgstr ""
"Acide chlorhydrique, aussi appelé acide muriatique. C'est un acide puissant "
"qui a une odeur distincte, important et fréquemment utilisé depuis sa "
"découverte. Il a encore une multitude d'utilités."

#. ~ Description of "water purification tablet"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Intended for the clarification and disinfection of unsafe drinking water "
"while camping or travelling, this sodium dichloroisocyanurate-based "
"purification tablet removes dangerous contaminants using powerful "
"chemicals.  The label says to use one tablet per liter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nitric acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Nitric acid, a strong oxidant and an extremely corrosive material.  Mainly "
"used in the production of synthetic fertilizers, for the etching of circuit "
"boards, and in woodworking.  Remains quite useful both for making a vast "
"array of pyrotechnic and explosive agents and as a direct weapon: not many "
"beings enjoy being doused in nitric acid."
msgstr ""
"De l'acide nitrique, un oxydant puissant et extrêmement corrosif. "
"Principalement utilisé durant la production d'engrais synthétiques, pour "
"façonner des circuits électriques ainsi que du bois. Aussi remarquablement "
"utile pour fabriquer un sélection variée d'agents pyrotechniques et "
"explosifs mais aussi capable d'être utilisé comme une arme tel quel vu que "
"la plupart des choses que vous pourriez couvrir d'acide nitrique ne risquent "
"pas de trop apprécier."

#. ~ Description of "commercial fertilizer"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Nutrient-rich granules for plants."
msgstr "Des granules riches en nutriments conçues pour nourrir des plantes."

#. ~ Description of "cement powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Portland is most likely long gone, but its memory persists in cement.  This "
"ubiquitous binder can be used for all kinds of advanced masonry.  Just add "
"water."
msgstr ""
"Un liant très utile pour la maçonnerie. Il faut juste y ajouter de l'eau."

#. ~ Name of material
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json data/json/materials.json
msgid "RDX"
msgid_plural "RDX"
msgstr[0] "RDX"
msgstr[1] "RDX"
msgstr[2] "RDX"

#. ~ Description of "rocuronium"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Rocuronium bromide, a fast-acting muscle relaxant.  Used primarily in "
"emergency medicine because of its relative stability, it can serve as a "
"component of a balanced anesthesia in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Bromide de Rocuronium, un relaxant musculaire à action rapide. Utilisé "
"principalement en cas d'urgence grâce à sa raisonnable stabilité. Il peut "
"servir pour dépanner comme composant d'un anesthésiant équilibré."

#. ~ Description of "aluminum sulfate"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime.  "
"Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of "
"soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid, it "
"could be used to saturate soil with aluminum, causing all but the most "
"resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr ""
"Plusieurs cristaux de sulfate d'aluminium. Il sert notamment comme agent de "
"purification de l'eau et molluscicide. Avant le cataclysme cette substance "
"servait à ajuster l'acidité des sols et comme aditif pour certaines poudres "
"de cuisson. Mélangé à un acide puissant, vous pouvez l'utilisez pour saturer "
"une zone de sol en aluminium, empêchant toutes sauf les plus résistantes des "
"plantes de se développer."

#. ~ Description of "RDX"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX, or hexogen: a military-grade, shelf-"
"stable high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges, or mixed with scrap "
"to pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr ""
"Quelques cristaux blanchâtres de RDX, ou hexogène : un explosif de classe "
"militaire, soufflant et stable. Peut être moulé en charges formées, ou "
"mélangé avec de la ferraille pour poivrer la zone de shrapnels à haute-"
"vélocité."

#. ~ Description of "bleach"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Sodium hypochlorite, a common household cleaning agent."
msgstr "De l'hypochlorite de sodium, un agent de nettoyage domestique commun."

#. ~ Description of "uranium"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Some uranium.  You should probably get very far away from this, if you enjoy "
"not being irradiated."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau d'uranium sans aucune protection. Vous devriez probablement "
"rester très loin de ceci si vous ne voulez pas être irradié(e)."

#. ~ Description of "liquid soap"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Standard skin-safe liquid soap, the type you might see on a kitchen sink, "
"shower shelf, or bathroom soap dispenser, but it should work reasonably well "
"for cleaning anything that's filthy."
msgstr ""
"Du savon standard non irritant, le type que vous pourriez trouver sur un "
"évier de cuisine, dans une douche ou dans des toilettes, devrait pouvoir "
"nettoyer quelque chose sale de façon satisfaisante."

#. ~ Description of "sulfuric acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Sulfuric acid: viscous, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, particularly "
"to organic matter and evil clowns.  Although used to prepare a number of "
"chemicals, it is mostly known as battery acid, due to its widest commercial "
"application."
msgstr ""
"Acide sulfurique: visqueux, nauséabond et très corrosif, particulièrement "
"avec les matières organiques et les mauvais clowns. Il est utilisé dans de "
"nombreuses formules chimiques mais est principalement connu pour son "
"utilisation en tant qu'acide de batterie."

#. ~ Description of "corpse ashes"
