#. ~ Description of "starry false Solomon's seal berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A bunch of deep red berries with a pleasant bittersweet flavor.  Can have a "
"laxative effect if eaten in large quantities."
msgstr ""
"Un poignée de baies au rouge profond ayant un goût doux-amer plaisant mais "
"ayant un effet laxatif avec une consommation excessive."

#. ~ Description of "handful of blackberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A darker cousin of the raspberry.  The color isn't actually what sets them "
"apart - the identifying characteristic is whether the stem stays connected "
"to the fruit when it's first picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "watermelon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A deep green melon, bigger than your head.  It is very juicy!  You should be "
"able to take it apart with a knife."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mango"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A fleshy tropical fruit with a large pit.  Better enjoy it soon, you're "
"pretty sure more of these aren't going to be imported for a long time."
msgstr ""
"Un fruit tropical juteux et sucré possédant un large noyau. Vous feriez "
"mieux d'en profiter vite vu qu'il est hautement improbable que qui que ce "
"soit en importe plus pour un bon moment."

#. ~ Description of "handful of chokeberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of black chokeberries.  They look similar to blackcurrant.  Big "
"and juicy but actually exceedingly sour."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of cantaloupe melon chunks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of cantaloupe melon chunks.  A great snack by itself or in a fruit "
"salad."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of coconut flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of coconut flesh.  It's surprisingly calorie-dense."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of nopales"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of edible pads from a cactus."
msgstr "Une poignée de morceaux de cactus comestibles."

#. ~ Description of "handful of elderberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of elderberries, toxic when eaten raw but great when cooked."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de baies de sureau, toxiques crues mais excellentes après "
"cuisson."

#. ~ Description of "handful of rose hips"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of fruits grown from pollinated rose flowers.  Full of irritating "
"hairs and hard seeds, they'll need to be disassembled before eating."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of huckleberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of huckleberries, often times confused for blueberries."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of grapes"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of juicy grapes.  Quite calorie-dense compared to most fruit, and "
"you might be able to make them into wine if you're ambitious enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of pineapple chunks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of pineapple chunks.  Delicious and a great source of Vitamin C, "
"though a bit sour."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of apricots"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of smooth-skinned fruits related to the peach."
msgstr "Un fruit rond à la peau douce de la même famille que la pêche."

#. ~ Description of "juice pulp"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of stringy pulp, left-over from juicing some kind of fruit.  It's "
"not very tasty, but contains a lot of healthy fiber."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de pulpe de fruits ayant été pressés. Pas vraiment agréable à "
"manger, mais pleine de fibres bonnes pour votre santé."

#. ~ Description of "handful of raspberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of sweet red berries, each with a hollow core."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wintergreen berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of sweet, brilliant red berries of the wintergreen shrub."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de baies sucrées et rondes issues d'une chimaphile, un petit "
"arbuste."

#. ~ Description of "handful of blueberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of tasty sweet-tart berries.  They're blue, but that doesn't mean "
"they're sad."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of strawberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of tasty, juicy red berries with visible seeds on the outside of "
"the skin.  Often found growing wild in fields."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de baies rouges, délicieuses et juteuses ayant des graines "
"visibles sur la peau. Celles-ci poussent souvent sans intervention humaine "
"dans des prairies."

#. ~ Description of "handful of cranberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of very bitter red berries, probably grown locally in "
"Massachusetts.  Good for urinary tract health."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "grapefruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A hybrid citrus fruit descended from the orange, whose taste ranges from "
"sour to semi-sweet, and a little bitter."
msgstr ""
"Un agrume hybride apparenté à l'orange au goût variant entre aigre et semi-"
"sucrée avec un après-goût légèrement amer."

#. ~ Description of "pear"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A juicy, bell-shaped pear.  Yum!"
msgstr "Une poire juteuse en forme de cloche. Miam!"

#. ~ Description of "cantaloupe melon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large and very sweet orange fruit.  Technically a berry, like all melons "
"are.  You should be able to take it apart with a knife."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large purple plum.  Tasty and good for your digestion."
msgstr "Une grosse prune violette. Bonne pour votre digestion et goûteuse."

#. ~ Description of "kiwi"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large, brown, and fuzzy-skinned berry.  Its delicious insides are green."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pineapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large, spiky tropical fruit.  A tough rind protects the tasty flesh "
"inside, and digging into it as-is would be pretty inefficient and messy.  "
"You should find a knife or something vaguely knife-like to cut it up with."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A leathery skin covers this purplish-brown little fruit.  It will need to be "
"deconstructed before anything can be done with it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "banana"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A long, curved yellow fruit in a peel.  Some people like using them in "
"desserts.  Those people are probably dead."
msgstr ""
"Un long fruit courbé et jaune, recouvert par une peau. Certaines personnes "
"aiment en manger au dessert. Ces personnes sont probablement mortes."

#. ~ Description of "mayapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A small, edible fruit of an otherwise toxic plant.  You should not eat too "
"many of them."
msgstr ""
"Un petit fruit comestible issu d'une plante autrement toxique. Vous devriez "
"probablement ne pas en abuser."

#. ~ Description of "orange"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet citrus fruit.  Also comes in juice form.  In case you were "
"wondering, the color is named after the fruit, not the other way around."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of cherries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet red fruit that grows on trees.  If you have some time on your hands, "
"maybe you could figure out how to do that trick where you tie a knot in the "
"stem with your tongue."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of passionfruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet, acidic fruit originating from South America.  It grows on vines and "
"is filled with seeds like a pomegranate.  Also known as the maracuya."
msgstr ""
"Un fruit acide et sucré issu d'Amérique du Sud et poussant sur des lianes. "
"Rempli de graines comme une grenade et aussi connu sous le nom de maracuya."

#. ~ Description of "guava"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet, sandy-textured fruit with pink flesh native to the Caribbean, "
"Central America, and South America.  Great for making milkshakes."
msgstr ""
"Un fruit sucré ayant une peau sableuse et de la chair rose originaire des "
"Caraïbes, ainsi que d'Amérique Centrale et Sud. Parfait pour un milkshake."

#. ~ Description of "crabapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A term used to describe both wild apples native to North America as well as "
"less appetizing feral varieties, these are rather small and far too sour."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "coconut"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A tropical fruit with a hard, hairy shell and a hollow inside full of liquid "
"and edible flesh.  If you want to eat it, you'll have to find something "
"heavy to crack open the shell and something sharp to remove the 'meat'."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lemon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A very sour citrus fruit.  Can be eaten if you're desperate, but you should "
"probably look for some other cooking application for this."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "papaya"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A very sweet and soft tropical fruit."
msgstr "Un fruit tropical doux et très sucré."

#. ~ Description of "watermelon wedge"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A yummy wedge of watermelon.  A handheld snack that tastes like summer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lulo"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"An acidic fruit found in South America and the Caribbean, it looks like a "
"hairy orange and is used mainly for juice and desserts.  Also known as the "
"naranjilla."
msgstr ""
"Un fruit acide originaire d'Amérique du Sud et des Caraïbes ayant "
"l'apparence d'une orange poilue et principalement utilisé pour son jus ou "
"comme ingrédient à dessert. Aussi connu sous le nom de naranjilla."

#. ~ Description of "apple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"An iconic and delicious fruit grown and enjoyed across the world, used for "
"generations in folk medicine as doctor repellant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "peeled mutant fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Divested of its skin, this mutated fruit is revealed to be a nonsensical "
"jumble of plant and animal matter.  Human hair and teeth grow from pithy "
"blood-slick flesh, redolent with the scent of rotting mangoes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of autumn olives"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Not tasting anything like olives, this sweet, red and very nutritious fruit "
"can also be used as a tomato-substitute in some cases."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of hobbleberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Some black hobbleberries.  They are quite sweet.  Before they ripened, they "
"were deceptively red and utterly bitter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of nannyberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Some dark blue nannyberries, tasting like prunes mixed with banana."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of tupelo fruits"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Some dark blue tupelo fruits.  They are tart and feature a hard seed but are "
"still enjoyable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut rose hips"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Tart little fruits grown from a rose bush, now separated from their inedible "
"seeds and spines."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cholla bud"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"The edible bud of a cholla cactus, with its spines removed; the candy of the "
"Mojave indigenous peoples.  Tastes similar to asparagus."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "peach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "This fruit's large pit is surrounded by its tasty flesh."
msgstr "Le gros noyau de ce fruit est entouré d'une chair savoureuse."

#. ~ Description of "handful of mulberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"This red variety of mulberries is unique to eastern North America, and is "
"said to have the strongest flavor of any variety in the world."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pomegranate"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Under this pomegranate's spongy skin lie hundreds of fleshy seeds."
msgstr ""

