#. ~ Description of "curry powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"A blend of spices meant to be used in some South Asian dishes.  Can't be "
"eaten raw, why would you even try that?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Italian seasoning"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "A fragrant mix of dried oregano, basil, thyme and other spices."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange parfumé d'herbes séchées : origan, basilic, thym, entre autres."

#. ~ Description of "mustard powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "A fragrant yellow powder.  Not edible in this form."
msgstr ""
"Une poudre jaune à l'arome fort, ce n'est probablement pas une bonne idée de "
"la consommer sous cette forme."

#. ~ Description of "thyme"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "A stalk of thyme.  Smells delicious."
msgstr "Une tige de thym. Ça sent très bon."

#. ~ Description of "wild herbs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"A tasty collection of wild herbs including violet, sassafras, mint, clover, "
"purslane, and fireweed."
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble délicieux d'herbes sauvages comprenant: violette, sassafras, "
"menthe, trèfle, pourpier, et bardane."

#. ~ Description of "chili powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Chili P, yo!  Not edible on its own, but it could be used to make seasoning."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hot sauce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Flamin' hot sauce.  It'd be a bad idea to drink it on its own.  You should "
"probably wash your hands after handling it, too."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "garlic powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Garlic that has been dehydrated and ground into a powder.  A must-have "
"seasoning in any pantry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "black pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "Ground black spice berries with a pungent aroma."
msgstr "Des grains d'épice noirs à l'arôme âcre."

#. ~ Description of "cinnamon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "Ground cinnamon bark with a sweet but slightly spicy aroma."
msgstr "Écorce de cannelle avec une douce mais légèrement épicée."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "Italian seasoning"
msgid_plural "Italian seasoning"
msgstr[0] "herbe de Provence"
msgstr[1] "herbes de Provence"
msgstr[2] "herbes de Provence"

#. ~ Description of "sprinkles"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Known as nonpareils, sprinkles, jimmies, sugar strands or 'hundreds-and-"
"thousands', these colorful balls, rods or flakes of sugar and starch are "
"intended for use decorating soft surfaces of sweets.  Like sugar, they are "
"bad for your teeth and surprisingly not very tasty on their own."
msgstr ""
"Connus sous le nom de nonpareils, de paillettes, de jimmies, de brins de "
"sucre ou de \"centaines et milliers\", ces boules, tiges ou flocons de sucre "
"et d'amidon colorés sont destinés à décorer les surfaces molles des bonbons. "
"Comme le sucre, ils sont mauvais pour les dents et, étonnamment, ils ne sont "
"pas très savoureux en eux-mêmes."

#. ~ Description of "seasoned salt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "Salt mixed with a fragrant blend of secret herbs and spices."
msgstr "Du sel mélangé avec un mélange parfumé  d'herbes secrètes et d'épices."

#. ~ Description of "soy sauce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid "Salty fermented soybean sauce."
msgstr "Une sauce salée de fèves de soja fermentées."

#. ~ Description of "spicebush berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Small, red berries with a pungent aroma.  It is said they are comparable to "
"allspice, but also boasting their own flavor profile."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sugar"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Sweet, sweet sugar.  Bad for your teeth and surprisingly not very tasty on "
"its own."
msgstr ""
"Douceur sucrée. Mauvais pour les dents. Étonnamment moins bon sans "
"accompagnement."

#. ~ Description of "artificial sweetener"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Sweet, sweet sugar?  No, it is bitter-sweet artificial sweetener.  No "
"calories, no worries."
msgstr ""
"Du sucre doux et sucré ? Non, c'est un édulcorant artificiel au goût doux-"
"amer. Pas de calories, pas d'inquiétudes."

#. ~ Description of "dry spicebush berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"These formerly red berries now have a stronger aroma after being dehydrated."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "salt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/spice.json
msgid ""
"Yuck!  You surely wouldn't want to eat this.  It's good for preserving meat "
"and cooking, though."
msgstr ""
"Vous n'allez quand même pas manger ça! C'est utile pour cuisiner ou "
"conserver la viande."

