#. ~ Description of "stone axe head"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A broad piece of stone with an edge narrow enough to roughly chop wood."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "metal axe head"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of steel with one edge hammered down to something resembling a "
"cutting edge.  It works passably well, but really can't compare to a proper "
"axe."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A hefty two-handed axe normally used by firefighters.  It makes a powerful "
"melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings.  Thanks to its "
"prying head, it can also be used to force locked doors and windows open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "street sign"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A large street sign, its aluminum pole uprooted.  An unreasonably strong "
"person might be able to wield it like a crude axe."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wood axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is a bit "
"slow to recover between swings."
msgstr ""
"Une grande hache à deux mains conçues pour abattre des arbres et fendre des "
"bûches. Une bonne arme de mêlée, mais un peu lente à asséner des coups avec "
"et épuisante à manier."

#. ~ Description of "hatchet"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A one-handed hatchet.  Makes a great melee weapon, and is useful both for "
"chopping things and hammering them."
msgstr ""
"Une hachette pouvant être confortablement maniée avec une main. Une très "
"bonne arme de mêlée et très capable d'à la fois couper des choses ou de les "
"marteler avec son plat."

#. ~ Description of "copper hatchet"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A primitive axe made from a small wedge of copper affixed to a short haft."
msgstr ""
"Une hache primitive fabriquée à partir d'un morceau affuté de cuivre attaché "
"à un manche en bois court."

#. ~ Description of "crash axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A short, lightweight emergency tool with a quarter-circular blade, a short "
"pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop "
"down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A socketed bronze axe with a work-hardened edge, tightly bound to the shaft "
"with cords."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stone adze"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A stone adze, a primitive tool for smoothing or scraping wood objects."
msgstr ""
"Une herminette en pierre, un outil primitif utilisé pour lisser ou gratter "
"des objets en bois."

#. ~ Description of "stone axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A stone with a narrow edge affixed to a stick.  It can chop wood, but "
"requires much more effort than a modern axe."
msgstr ""
"Un pierre ayant un côté un peu tranchant ayant été attachée à un bâton. Vous "
"pourriez couper du bois avec, mais cela demanderait beaucoup plus d'effort "
"qu'avec une hache moderne."

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"An axe designed for medieval warfare, the head secured to the haft with "
"langets.  Though formidable, it's lighter than the sort you'd use for "
"felling trees, and would make an inferior tool for that purpose."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr ""

