#. ~ Description of monster "moorhen"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A bird belonging to the Rallidae family.  They are relatives of the coots "
"but have a distinctive red coloration on their heads and brownish plumage."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau appartenant à la famille des Rallidées. Ils sont apparentés aux "
"foulques mais ont une coloration rouge distinctive sur la tête et un plumage "
"brunâtre."

#. ~ Description of monster "coot"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A bird belonging to the Rallidae family.  They can be found worldwide on "
"freshwater habitats, including many islands in the not so distant past."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau appartenant à la famille des Rallidées. On les trouve partout dans "
"le monde, dans des habitats d’eau douce, y compris sur de nombreuses îles "
"dans un passé pas si lointain."

#. ~ Description of monster "robin"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A brown songbird with a reddish-orange breast.  Their eggs are a distinctive "
"shade of blue."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau chanteur brun avec une poitrine rouge-orange. Leurs œufs sont "
"d'une nuance de bleu distinctive."

#. ~ Description of monster "grouse"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A common game bird resembling a quail or a very small chicken."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "scavenger crow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A crow or raven grown three or four times bigger than ought to be possible.  "
"Its sharp beak, vicious talons, and insatiable hunger make it a threat to "
"the living and the dead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "chicken"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A domesticated descendant of junglefowl, it may still be the most numerous "
"bird in the world.  Before the Cataclysm, it was raised by humans as a "
"source of meat, eggs, and early morning wakeup calls."
msgstr ""
"Un descendant domestiqué du coq sauvage, et peut être encore l'oiseau le "
"plus répandu au monde. Avant le Cataclysme celui-ci était élevé pour sa "
"viande, ses œufs et son cri matinal distinctif."

#. ~ Description of monster "crow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A fairly large, elegant black bird, famous for its distinctive call.  An "
"intelligent bird, there is a glitter of mischief behind its eyes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "pigeon"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A gentle, plump, small-billed bird with a skin saddle, or cere, between its "
"bill and forehead.  On the ground, it struts about with a characteristic "
"bobbing of the head.  It is a strong, swift flier thanks to its long wings "
"and powerful flight muscles."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau doux, dodu, à petit bec, avec une cire entre le bec et le front. "
"Au sol, il se pavane avec un mouvement de tête caractéristique. C'est un "
"oiseau fort et rapide grâce à ses longues ailes et ses puissants muscles de "
"vol."

#. ~ Description of monster "turkey"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A large and colorful game bird native to the forests of North America.  Its "
"head and beak are covered in fleshy protuberances."
msgstr ""
"Un grand gibier à plume coloré originaire des forêts d'Amérique du Nord. Sa "
"tête et son bec sont couverts de protubérances charnues"

#. ~ Description of monster "duck"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A mallard duck, often seen around rivers and other bodies of water.  It "
"feeds primarily on insects, seeds, roots, and, pre-Cataclysm, bread scraps."
msgstr ""
"Un canard colvert, souvent observé autour des rivières et autres plans "
"d'eau. Il se nourrit principalement d’insectes, de graines, de racines et, "
"avant le Cataclysme, de restes de pain."

#. ~ Description of monster "grebe"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A medium sized aquatic bird with a long neck.  These birds can be "
"distinguished by their strange leg placement which makes them great at "
"diving."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau aquatique de taille moyenne avec un long cou. Ces oiseaux se "
"distinguent par le placement étrange de leurs pattes, ce qui les rend "
"excellents en plongée."

#. ~ Description of monster "pheasant"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A medium-sized game bird that can have bright feathers depending on the sex "
"and species."
msgstr ""
"Gibier à plumes de taille moyenne qui peut avoir des plumes brillantes selon "
"le sexe et l'espèce."

#. ~ Description of monster "sparrow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A small bird with brown and gray feathers.  Introduced to North America in "
"the 1850s, it is now one of the most abundant birds in the continent."
msgstr ""
"Un petit oiseau aux plumes brunes et grises. Introduit en Amérique du Nord "
"dans les années 1850, c'est aujourd'hui l'un des oiseaux les plus abondants "
"du continent."

#. ~ Description of monster "woodpecker"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A small bird with woody colors and a colored crest on its head.  These birds "
"are well known for their ability to poke holes on trees while looking for "
"grubs."
msgstr ""
"Un petit oiseau aux couleurs boisées et avec une crête colorée sur la tête. "
"Ces oiseaux sont bien connus pour leur capacité à percer des trous dans les "
"arbres tout en recherchant des larves."

#. ~ Description of monster "cardinal"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A small songbird, famous for its distinctive crest and facial markings.  A "
"well-known example of sexual dimorphism, the males are colored much more "
"vibrantly than the females."
msgstr ""
"Un petit oiseau chanteur, célèbre pour sa crête distinctive et ses marques "
"faciales. Exemple bien connu de dimorphisme sexuel, les mâles ont des "
"couleurs beaucoup plus vives que les femelles."

#. ~ Description of monster "raven"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A small, elegant black bird, famous for its distinctive call.  A clever "
"bird, there is a glitter of mischief behind its eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un petit oiseau noir élégant, célèbre pour son cri très distinct. Un animal "
"très intelligent avec des yeux remplis de malice."

#. ~ Description of monster "blue jay"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small, noisy bird with distinctive blue feathers."
msgstr "Un petit oiseau bruyant aux plumes bleues distinctives."

#. ~ Description of monster "brown chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A tiny darkly-colored chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr ""
"Il s’agit d’un petit poussin de couleur foncée, il pourrait s'agir de "
"plusieurs espèces différentes."

#. ~ Description of monster "grey chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A tiny dull-colored chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow chick"
#. ~ Description of monster "mon_grouse_chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A tiny yellow and brown chick, it could be from a number of different "
"species."
msgstr ""
"Un petit poussin jaune et brun, il pourrait s'agir de plusieurs espèces "
"différentes."

#. ~ Description of monster "waterfowl chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"A tiny yellow and brown waterfowl chick, it could be from a number of "
"different species."
msgstr ""
"Petit poussin de sauvagine jaune et brun, il pourrait s'agir de plusieurs "
"espèces différentes."

#. ~ Description of monster "goose"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A waterfowl well known for its loud honking and aggressive behavior."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "cormorant"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid ""
"An aquatic bird with a long snake-like neck.  They are considered coastal "
"birds but many species can also be found on freshwater habitats."
msgstr ""
"Un oiseau aquatique avec un long cou en forme de serpent. Ils sont "
"considérés comme des oiseaux côtiers, mais de nombreuses espèces peuvent "
"également être trouvées dans les habitats d'eau douce."

