msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "kokanee salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A Kokanee salmon.  A very fatty, nutritious fish.  Tastes great smoked."
msgstr ""
"Un saumon kokani. Un poisson très gras et nourrissant. Excellent une fois "
"fumé. "

#. ~ Description of monster "banded sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A banded sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "Un crapet à bandes, un cousin des bars."

#. ~ Description of monster "black crappie"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A black crappie.  A medium-sized fish also known as a 'calico bass'."
msgstr ""
"Une marigane noire, un poisson de taille moyenne aussi connu sous le nom de "
"basse calico."

#. ~ Description of monster "bluegill"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A bluegill, an invasive species in Japan.  Commonly gutted and cooked whole."
msgstr "Un crapet arlequin. Habituellement vidé puis cuit entier."

#. ~ Description of monster "bowfin"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A bowfin.  These fish are related to gar but without the huge teeth, skin-"
"rending scales, and aggression."
msgstr ""
"Un poisson-castor, un cousin du brochet dépourvu de son agressivité, de ses "
"dents pointues, écailles coupantes, mais ayant reçu en compensation une tête "
"couverte de longues plaques osseuses."

#. ~ Description of monster "brook trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A brook trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for "
"the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr ""
"Une truite mouchetée. Une prise populaire durant les weekends de pêche entre "
"père et fils, le vidage étant moins agréable."

#. ~ Description of monster "brown bullhead"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A brown bullhead, a type of catfish.  Delicious when battered and fried."
msgstr ""
"Une barbotte brune, une espèce de poisson chat délicieuse panée et frite."

#. ~ Description of monster "brown trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A brown trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for "
"the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr ""
"Une truite brune. Une prise populaire durant les weekends de pêche entre "
"père et fils, le vidage étant moins agréable."

#. ~ Description of monster "chain pickerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A chain pickerel.  It looks like a pike, but slightly smaller."
msgstr "Une espèce de brochet plus petite que la normale."

#. ~ Description of monster "channel catfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A channel catfish.  It has a forked tail and long whiskers."
msgstr ""
"Une barbue de rivière, une espèce de poisson chat possédant une queue "
"fourchue et de longues moustaches."

#. ~ Description of monster "lobster"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A dark greenish crustacean in its natural habitat.  These were once "
"considered pests barely worth eating, then some marketing genius started "
"selling them to people as a delicacy and they took off in popularity… and "
"price."
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé noir verdâtre dans son habitat naturel. Autrefois considérés "
"nuisibles et valant à peine d'être mangés, un génie du marketing décida un "
"jour de les vendre comme un met raffiné, causant ceux-ci à gagner en "
"popularité… et en prix."

#. ~ Description of monster "fallfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A fallfish.  These fish are small cyprinids, related to carp."
msgstr "Un ouitouche, un petit cyprinidé apparenté aux carpes."

#. ~ Description of monster "summer flounder"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A flatfish, the summer flounder, also known as a fluke, likes to stay "
"camouflaged against the ocean floor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "European carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A golden-yellow common carp.  Some people think they don't taste great, but "
"you can't afford to be choosy in the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Une carpe commune aux reflets dorés. Certains trouvent que ce poisson n'a "
"pas un goût terrible mais le Cataclysme ne vous laisse pas vraiment le luxe "
"du choix."

#. ~ Description of monster "green sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A green sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "Un crapet vert, un petit poisson cousin des bars."

#. ~ Description of monster "mutant fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A half-translucent fish larva… though this one is far larger than the "
"usual.  Impossible to identify which species it belongs to but you can "
"safely tell that it is going to outgrow normal fish you're used to seeing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "huge fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge fish."
msgstr "poisson d'énorme taille."

#. ~ Description of monster "grass carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge grass carp.  A golden, herbivorous fish."
msgstr "Une carpe de roseau, un poisson herbivore doré énorme."

#. ~ Description of monster "huge salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge mutant salmon grown almost to the size of an alligator."
msgstr ""
"Un saumon aux proportions démesurées ayant presque la taille d'un alligator "
"adulte."

#. ~ Description of monster "leaper salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A huge mutant salmon, one that outgrows even the other ones present.  On its "
"sides, beneath the fins, are visible two flesh-colored tubes which propel "
"water as it leaps."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "lake trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A lake trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for "
"the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr ""
"Une truite grise. Une prise populaire durant les weekends de pêche entre "
"père et fils, le vidage étant moins agréable."

#. ~ Description of monster "lake whitefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A lake whitefish, closely related to salmon.  One can assume they taste just "
"as nice when smoked."
msgstr ""
"Un grand corégone, un cousin proche du saumon, vous assumez qu'il à un goût "
"aussi bon que celui-ci fumé."

#. ~ Description of monster "longnose gar"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large ancient type of fish with a mean jaw and poisonous eggs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large crayfish larva already larger than non-mutated adults of its kind."
msgstr ""
"Une larve d'écrevisse mutante gigantesque déjà plus large que les adultes "
"non-mutants de son espèce."

#. ~ Description of monster "large fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large fish."
msgstr "Un poisson de large taille."

#. ~ Description of monster "seweranha"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large, mutant variety of carp.  It has shimmering green scales and a mouth "
"lined with three jagged rows of razor-sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Un carpe mutante doté d'écailles vert luisant et d'une gueule bordée de "
"trois rangées de dents aiguisées comme des rasoirs."

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic cod"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large, white-meat fish known for its mild flavor and flaky texture.  "
"Highly prized in both commercial and recreational fishing."
msgstr ""
"Un poisson à la viande blanche pouvant atteindre une taille impressionnante, "
"la viande en question étant réputé pour sa saveur douce et sa texture "
"feuilletée. Une prise préférée des pécheurs commerciaux et sportifs."

#. ~ Description of monster "largemouth bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A largemouth bass.  Very popular with sport fishermen."
msgstr "Un achigan à grande bouche. Très populaire avec les pêcheurs sportifs."

#. ~ Description of monster "razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A man-sized crustacean clad in iron-like chitin, capable of emitting "
"horrible shrieking noises.  Often spotted near shipwrecks or other dark, "
"damp places, which it uses as nesting grounds."
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé mutant de la taille d'un homme adulte possédant une carapace en "
"chitine épaisse et très résistante, capable d'émettre des crissements "
"horribles avec ses mandibules. Cet monstruosité préfère fréquenter les "
"épaves ou autres endroits similairement humides et sombres pouvant être "
"utilisés comme sites de ponte."

#. ~ Description of monster "medium fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A medium fish."
msgstr "Un poisson de taille moyenne."

#. ~ Description of monster "pollock"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A member of the cod family, pollock is a versatile fish known for its white, "
"delicate meat and mild taste."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de la famille de la morue, la goberge est un poisson versatile "
"connu pour sa viande blanche est délicate au goût léger."

#. ~ Description of monster "crustacean larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A minuscule half-translucent crustacean larva.  Impossible to identify which "
"species it belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Une larve de crustacé presque translucide, il est complètement impossible "
"d'identifier précisement à quelle espèce elle appartient."

#. ~ Description of monster "fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A minuscule half-translucent fish larva.  Impossible to identify which "
"species it belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Une alevin miniscule presque translucide. Vous auriez beaucoup de mal à "
"distinguer à quel espèce il appartient avant que celui-ci devienne un peu "
"plus large."

#. ~ Description of monster "muskellunge"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A muskellunge.  Closely related to pike but even larger, it shares the same "
"aggression and sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Un maskinongé. Apparenté au brochet mais encore plus gros, et partageant son "
"agressivité et ses dents pointues."

#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutant crayfish the size of a dog, with a brown carapace, claws, and long "
"antennae."
msgstr ""
"Une écrevisse mutante de la taille d'un chien possédant une carapace brune, "
"des pinces menaçantes et de longues antennes."

#. ~ Description of monster "alpha razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutated crustacean the size of a horse.  With its bulky body and sword-"
"like pincers, it serves as a protector of the nest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutated salmon roughly the size of a person.  Quite dangerous to the "
"inexperienced angler."
msgstr ""
"Un saumon mutant de la taille d'une personne et très dangereux pour le "
"pêcheur du dimanche."

#. ~ Description of monster "northern pike"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A northern pike.  Pike can be pretty aggressive fish, careful around those "
"teeth."
msgstr ""
"Un brochet du nord, un poisson assez agressif, donc attention à ne pas vous "
"faire mordre."

#. ~ Description of monster "haddock"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A popular food fish, the haddock is recognized by its dark lateral line and "
"a black blotch above the pectoral fin."
msgstr ""
"Un poisson populaire pour sa viande, l'aiglefin est distingué par une longue "
"ligne latérale sombre et une tache noire au dessus de ses nageoires "
"pectorales."

#. ~ Description of monster "pumpkinseed"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A pumpkinseed sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "Une perche soleil, un petit poisson cousin des crapets et des bars."

#. ~ Description of monster "rainbow trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A rainbow trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except "
"for the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr ""
"Une truite arc-en-ciel. Une prise populaire durant les weekends de pêche "
"entre père et fils, le vidage étant moins agréable."

#. ~ Description of monster "redbreast sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A redbreast sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "Un crapet rouge, un petit poisson cousin des bars."

#. ~ Description of monster "burbot"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A relatively large fish that looks like a cross between a catfish and an "
"eel, and is the only freshwater fish from the order that cods hail from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "rock bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A rock bass.  Related to sunfish, this tiny fish has a camouflage-like "
"patterning and red eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un crapet de roche, techniquement plus un bar qu'un crapet, ce tout petit "
"poisson est muni d'un motif de peau camouflage et d'yeux rouges."

#. ~ Description of monster "round whitefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A round whitefish, closely related to salmon.  One can assume they taste "
"just as nice when smoked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "small fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A small fish."
msgstr "Un petit poisson."

#. ~ Description of monster "black sea bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A small, robust fish, the black sea bass is known for its dark, mottled "
"color and meaty texture."
msgstr ""
"Un petit poisson robuste, le bar noir est connu pour ses couleurs sombres "
"tachées et la texture charnue de sa viande."

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow perch"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A small, sprightly perch.  It is a very bony fish, still has some tasty meat "
"on it though."
msgstr ""
"Une perchaude, un petit poisson vif, bourré d'arrêtes mais pas mal à manger."

#. ~ Description of monster "smallmouth bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A smallmouth bass.  Infamously intolerant to pollution, the presence of "
"smallmouth bass is a good indicator of how clean a body of water is."
msgstr ""
"Un achigan à petite bouche, un poisson notoirement susceptible à la "
"pollution de son environment, son absence étant un mauvais signe pour la "
"qualité d'un plan d'eau."

#. ~ Description of monster "striped bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A striped bass.  Mostly a saltwater fish, they migrate to fresher water to "
"spawn."
msgstr ""
"Un bar rayé. Normalement un poisson d'eau salé, il effectue une migration "
"dans des eaux plus douces pour se reproduire."

#. ~ Description of monster "tiny fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A tiny fish."
msgstr "Un poisson miniscule."

#. ~ Description of monster "lake sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A very large armored bottom-feeder, the lake sturgeon is one of the largest "
"unmutated fish one can find in the freshwater regions of New England."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "walleye"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A walleye.  A green-brown medium-sized fish with a white belly."
msgstr ""
"Un doré jaune, un poisson de taille moyenne possédant un ventre blanchâtre."

#. ~ Description of monster "warmouth"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A warmouth, similar to a rock bass.  This small fish is related to the "
"sunfish."
msgstr "Un crapet sac-à-lait, proche cousin du crapet de roche."

#. ~ Description of monster "white catfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A white catfish.  A small whiskered fish with a broad head."
msgstr ""
"Un poisson chat blanc possédant des moustaches courtes et une tête large."

#. ~ Description of monster "white sucker"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A white sucker.  It has a streamlined body with a round mouth."
msgstr "Un meunier blanc. Il a un corps profilé avec une bouche ronde."

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow bullhead"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A yellow bullhead, a type of catfish.  Delicious when battered and fried, "
"though smaller than its brown cousin."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "scup"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"Also known as porgy, the scup is a small fish commonly found in Atlantic "
"coastal waters, recognizable by its silver body with blue and purple tinges."
msgstr ""
"Le pagre est un petit poisson commun dans les eau côtières de l'Atlantique, "
"reconnaissable par sa peau argentée teintée de bleu et de violet."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American eel"
msgid_plural "American eels"
msgstr[0] "anguille américaine"
msgstr[1] "anguilles américaines"
msgstr[2] "anguilles américaines"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American pickerel"
msgid_plural "American pickerels"
msgstr[0] "chabot américain"
msgstr[1] "chabots américains"
msgstr[2] "chabots américains"

#. ~ Description of monster "American eel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An American eel.  They used to be quite common in these parts until the dams "
"were built.  They'll get a second chance now that those aren't running."
msgstr ""
"Une anguille américaine, commune dans les environs avant la construction de "
"masse de barrages, mais sa population va peut être rebondir maintenant que "
"ceux-ci ne fonctionnent plus."

#. ~ Description of monster "American pickerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An American pickerel.  It looks like a pike, but unlike its chain pickerel "
"cousin, this one is way smaller."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic mackerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An Atlantic mackerel, known for its distinctive striped pattern."
msgstr "Un maquereau bleu célèbre pour ses rayures distinctives."

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An Atlantic salmon.  A very fatty, nutritious fish.  Tastes great smoked."
msgstr ""
"Un saumon d'Atlantique. Un poisson très gras et nourrissant. Excellent une "
"fois fumé. "

#. ~ Description of monster "colossal crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An enormous mutated gray crayfish with pincer claws and long antennae."
msgstr ""
"Une écrevisse mutante énorme munie de pinces redoutables et de longues "
"antennes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid_plural "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgstr[0] "thon rouge du nord"
msgstr[1] "thons rouges du nord"
msgstr[2] "thons rouges du nord"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic cod"
msgid_plural "Atlantic cod"
msgstr[0] "morue franche"
msgstr[1] "morues franches"
msgstr[2] "morues franches"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic halibut"
msgid_plural "Atlantic halibut"
msgstr[0] "flétan atlantique"
msgstr[1] "flétans atlantiques"
msgstr[2] "flétans atlantiques"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic mackerel"
msgid_plural "Atlantic mackerel"
msgstr[0] "maquereau bleu"
msgstr[1] "maquereaus bleus"
msgstr[2] "maquereaus bleus"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic salmon"
msgid_plural "Atlantic salmon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "European carp"
msgid_plural "European carp"
msgstr[0] "carpe européenne"
msgstr[1] "carpes européennes"
msgstr[2] "carpes européennes"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"One of the largest and fastest fish in the waters of New England, the "
"bluefin tuna is a streamlined predator with a dark blue back and silvery "
"sides."
msgstr ""
"L'un des plus gros et véloces poissons dans les eaux de la Nouvelle "
"Angleterre, le thons rouges du nord est un prédateur profilé aux flancs "
"argentés bleu sombre."

#. ~ Description of monster "lakebed creeper"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"Pink and translucent, with all of its otherworldly organs visible through "
"its skin, this meter-high conical creature creeps along the seabed with its "
"stubby, furry legs.  It contracts some kind of retracted barbed filaments "
"into an orifice at its rear as it aims it at potential prey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Death message of monster "fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#, c-format
msgid "The %s is smashed to non-recognizable pieces."
msgstr "L'%s est écrabouillé en un nuage de chair et de sang."

#. ~ Description of monster "bluefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"The bluefish, a moderately proportioned marine fish, is known for its "
"aggressive nature and sharp teeth.  It sports a distinct blue-green "
"coloration."
msgstr ""
"Un tassergals, un poisson océanique aux proportions respectables ayant un "
"tempérament agressif et des dents pointues. Sa peau est teintée bleu-vert."

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic halibut"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"The largest flatfish in the ocean, known for its dense, firm texture and "
"mild flavor."
msgstr ""
"Le plus gros poissons plats océanique, réputé pour la texture dense et ferme "
"de sa viande et la saveur douce de celle-ci."

#. ~ Description of monster "crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This crustacean looks like a tiny lobster, but is actually a completely "
"different species.  If you could get ahold of a bunch more of these, a hefty "
"pot of boiling water, and some spicy seasonings…"
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé ayant l'air d'un homard miniature, et très bon cuit dans une "
"marmite avec des épices."

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "This crustacean, larger than a man, resembles a mud-colored lobster."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This thing looks like a carp, but huge and very, very angry.  Death is the "
"gift of the carp god."
msgstr ""
"Cette chose à l'apparence d'une carpe, mais absolument gigantesque et "
"vraiment, vraiment très susceptible, votre mort sera une bonne offrande pour "
"le dieu des carpes."

#. ~ Description of monster "shortnose sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"While the shortnose sturgeon is still large, it is nothing compared to its "
"cousin - the lake sturgeon.  What really sets it apart, however, is its "
"signature shorter snout."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "goldfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"Yes, this is that common pet fish.  Though, given its size and the fact that "
"it's still alive, you can take a wild guess that this one is feral."
msgstr ""

