#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#, c-format
msgid "The %s softly purrs as you pet it.  It demands more."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "black bear"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The American black bear.  A large omnivorous scavenger, it has powerful "
"claws and jaws, and is an effective ambush hunter.  Most individuals are shy "
"around humans, but they're fiercely protective of their cubs."
msgstr ""
"L'ours noir d'Amérique. Un imposant omnivore doté d'une mâchoire et des "
"griffes puissantes en faisant un chasseur d'embuscade efficace. Bien qu'il "
"soit assez redoutable pour poser un réel danger à l'homme, il préfère "
"l'éviter généralement."

#. ~ Description of monster "mink"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The American mink, a partially aquatic weasel, once factory-farmed for its "
"fur.  It is a capable fisher, but the presence of otters in these parts "
"makes it rely more on food from the land."
msgstr ""
"Le vison américain, une belette partiellement aquatique ayant autrefois été "
"élevée intensément pour sa fourrure. C'est un pêcheur compétent mais la "
"présence de loutre sur son territoire en Nouvelle Angleterre le rends plus "
"terrestre."

#. ~ Description of monster "coyote"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Eastern coyote, also called the tweed wolf, is a territorial canine "
"descended from the offspring of gray wolves and true coyotes.  It is "
"intimidated by humans and other predators, but it will still fight if "
"threatened, and the Cataclysm has made it more fearless than usual."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Eastern moose, the largest living species of deer.  Though herbivorous, "
"these powerful animals can be dangerous if approached, especially during "
"mating season."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "beaver"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The North American beaver, the continent's largest rodent.  Its paddle-"
"shaped tail helps ferry it through the water, and its prominent teeth can "
"chew through wood, which it uses to build dam-like nests in lakes and "
"streams."
msgstr ""
"Le castor du Canada, le plus gros rongeur du continent. Sa queue en forme de "
"pagaie l'aide à nager; ses dents peuvent couper du bois qu'il utilise pour "
"fabriquer des nids en forme de barrages sur les lacs et cours d'eau."

#. ~ Description of monster "otter"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The North American river otter, a shy water-dwelling relative of the weasel "
"that lives in large families along the banks of streams.  It is an excellent "
"fisher and a resourceful survivor, using the abandoned dens of beavers and "
"other animals to raise its own young."
msgstr ""
"Une loutre de rivière nord américaine, une cousine timide de la belette "
"vivant en larges groupes en bord de rivière. Une excellente pêcheuse mais "
"n'hésitant pas à varier son alimentation si l'opportunité se présente et "
"utilisant parfois des barrages de castor abandonnés pour abriter leurs "
"propres petits."

#. ~ Description of monster "lemming"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Northern bog lemming, a small, predominantly vegetarian rodent that "
"spends its life in the murk of swamps and other wetlands.  Contrary to "
"popular belief, these creatures are not particularly hapless or suicidal, "
"but they can eat themselves into scarcity within a few generations."
msgstr ""
"Un petit rongeur végétarien qui passe sa vie dans les marais et la toundra. "
"Contrairement aux légendes urbaines, ils ne sont pas suicidaires, mais "
"peuvent se manger entre eux dans les grandes périodes de sécheresse."

#. ~ Description of monster "opossum"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Virginia opossum, a small omnivorous marsupial native to North America.  "
"About the size of a cat, it is hardy and adaptive, and a fairly common sight "
"in urban areas."
msgstr ""
"L'opossum de Virginie, un petit marsupial omnivore natif d'Amérique du nord. "
"Mesurant à peu près la taille d'un chat, il est résistant et s'adapte; on le "
"croise souvent dans les zones urbaines."

#. ~ Description of monster "moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf.  They can outrun a human within days of "
"birth and gain weight at an incredible pace."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "skunk"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The common striped skunk, similar in size to opossum or domestic cats, these "
"mammals can often be smelled before they are seen."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "cow"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The domestic cow, a baleful, ruminating farm animal.  She is quite muscular, "
"and would be a great source of milk if domesticated or of meat and leather "
"if slaughtered."
msgstr ""
"Une vache domestique, un animal de ferme ruminant. Assez musclée, vous "
"pourriez en tirer un bon rendement de viande en l'abattant ou la garder pour "
"son lait en la domestiquant."

#. ~ Description of monster "calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The domestic cow, a baleful, ruminating farm animal.  This one is still a "
"juvenile; it'll take a while before you can get any milk or a meaningful "
"amount of meat from her."
msgstr ""
"Une vache domestique, un animal de ferme ruminant. Celle-ci est toujours "
"juvénile et il vous faudra un bon moment pour espérer tirer un bon rendement "
"de lait ou de viande d'elle."

#. ~ Description of monster "chipmunk"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The eastern chipmunk, a tiny omnivorous rodent with a characteristic striped "
"coat.  It spends much of the day patrolling its elaborate burrow and the "
"precious stores of foraged food within."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "weasel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The long-tailed weasel, a small but ubiquitous predator whose range extends "
"across the continent.  It forms its den in small burrows, preferring to "
"occupy the nesting holes of its prey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "tiger"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The majestic tiger, a large feline predator.  Native to Asia, they are now "
"most populous in private reserves in the United States.  Fast and powerful, "
"this predator is one of the most recognizable and beloved animals in the "
"world.  Also one of the deadliest."
msgstr ""
"Un tigre majestueux, ce grand félin originaire d'Asie était assez répandu à "
"travers les réserves animales et zoo américains avant le Cataclysme. Ce "
"prédateur est phénoménalement rapide et fort, et n'hésitera pas à vous "
"inclure dans son diner."

#. ~ Description of monster "deer"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The northern woodland white-tailed deer, a quick and strong grazing animal.  "
"Favored prey of coyotes, wolves, and giant spider mutants."
msgstr ""
"Un cerf des bois du nord. Fort et rapide. Il est la proie favorite des "
"coyotes et des araignées mutantes géantes."

#. ~ Description of monster "attack dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"This average-sized dog has clearly had some training.  It is toned and "
"attentive, and seems likely to respond with aggression."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "lame horse"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Violence or misadventure has left this animal in a sorry state.  Unable to "
"walk, the horse lies on one side, wheezing in pain as it awaits the "
"inevitable."
msgstr ""

