msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"That ain't the point here, chum.  Don'tcha get it?  This was MY territory, "
"but they took it away from me.  Now they think of us as nothin' but a "
"<swear> nuisance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "That's understandable."
msgstr "C'est compréhensible"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"They are nice people, lettin' us stay here 'n all.  I got friends here, and "
"while we may not be members we belong here.  We'll fight together if they "
"ever try to kick us out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "What nightmare?"
msgstr "Quel cauchemar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Who I was is gone, dead… died when I put down the monsters wearing the face "
"of my friends.  Ever since then, I've felt nothing but disgust for myself.  "
"Let's not <swear> reminisce."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Why don't you blow this joint and come with me?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid "Alright, let's chat."
msgstr "Ok, discutons."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Could I have some food?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je pourrais avoir à manger?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"Could be better, could be worse, but I'm not complaining.  I have everything "
"I need here; my family, a nice job, and roof over my head.  I only wish God "
"was as forgiving to others as to me."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Jeremiah?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Katherine?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Jeremiah?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Katherine?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Good to hear that."
msgstr "Ça fait plaisir à attendre."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Hello stranger, I don't think we've met before.  Its nice to meet you, "
"name's Simon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Hello stranger, I don't think we've met before.  Its nice to meet you, "
"name's Simon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Hello stranger, I don't think we've met before.  Its nice to meet you, "
"name's Simon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "How are you holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "I gotta go, see you later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "I guess I'll starve."
msgstr "Je suppose que je vais mourir de faim."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "I heard the joinees could get some food here."
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu que les nouveaux arrivants pouvaient reçevoir à manger ici."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"I used to volunteer as a cook in a homeless shelter.  I met the church "
"through that job; their missionaries would come by every so often and hand "
"out essentials to people living there, then give a sermon in one of the back "
"rooms.  Katherine and I wound up going to one of their sermons, and we've "
"stayed connected since.  Working in that shelter taught me to cook on a "
"shoestring budget; that's really useful these days, ya know."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Snippet in category "<done_conversation_section>"
#. ~ Avatar response to an NPC that can be used for TALK_NONE responses.  Could be used in a lot more dialogs.  Could also use a lot more variety.
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "I'd like to ask you about something else."
msgstr "Je voudrais vous demander autre chose."

#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.  Comes up a lot and could use more variety.
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "I'll do that."
msgstr "Je ferais ça."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "I've changed my mind, forget about it."
msgstr "J'ai changé(e) d'avis, oubliez."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Is there any way I could join the community?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "It was worth a shot, I guess."
msgstr "Ça valait le coup d'essayer je suppose."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"It's been a while since anyone gave out meals.  We're low on supplies around "
"here, I can't spare any.  I'm sorry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"Jeremiah is my son, he's a sweet boy and all grown up now.  We taught him "
"everything he knows, and we all had high hopes for how he could make it in "
"the world, before <the_cataclysm> took it away.  He doesn't like his mother, "
"Katherine, very much, and I've tried to help the two, but they can't seem to "
"properly get along."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Just passing through, don't mind me."
msgstr "Je ne fait que passer, ne me faites pas trop attention."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"Katherine is a bit overprotective of him, and ever since <the_cataclysm>, "
"she's become extremely worried for his safety.  He wants more independence, "
"seein' as how he's grown now, but she won't leave him be.  She tells me that "
"someone needs to keep an eye on him, so she took it upon herself to do so.  "
"I think she has the best intentions at heart, I know she loves him dearly, "
"but the boy needs to figure out some things on his own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"Katherine's probably in the bunks right now, and Jeremiah's next door.  Feel "
"free to say hello sometime."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"Look, I have a family too.  I know how hard it is for you, but I've already "
"told you, rules are rules."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "No, I wouldn't.  Like I said, we don't have any to spare."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Okay, man.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Okay, shoot."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "On second thought, I gotta go.  See ya, <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Please?  I need it for my family."
msgstr "S'il vous plaît? J'en ai besoin pour ma famille."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"She's my wife, worked for the Church before <the_cataclysm>.  She used to "
"organize charities for the needy, now we're the ones in need of charity.  "
"She has a bit of a high horse these days, but a nice lady once you get to "
"know her.  We've been married for 28 years, and I couldn't ask for a better "
"wife."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Sure, what's up?"
msgstr "Ok, qu'est ce qu'il y a?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Thanks, <name_g>.  See you around."
msgstr "Merci, <name_g>. À plus tard."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "That's good to hear, but I gotta go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "That's good to hear.  I'd like to ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"They can, but we're limited on the portions for now.  Hope you enjoy it, and "
"come back tomorrow for another."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"This is the New England Community Church, I should say it's one of their old "
"retreats.  I'm Simon, the head chef around here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Where's your family now?"
msgstr "Où est votre famille en ce moment?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Who are you?  Where am I right now?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous? Où suis-je?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Who's Jeremiah?"
msgstr "Qui est Jeremiah?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Who's Katherine?"
msgstr "Qui est Katherine?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Why would they have an issue with each other?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid "Would you accept any money for it?"
msgstr "Vous accepteriez de l'argent en échange?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/cook.json
msgid ""
"You'd have to talk to Gemma or Julian about that.  I'm sure there's a way, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Vous allez devoir parler avec Gemma ou Julian pour ça. Je suis sûr qu'il "
"devrait y avoir un moyen pour vous d'arranger ça par contre."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Alright then, fuck you <name_b>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Alright, alright.  Here's some food and water, <name_b>.  Get out of my "
"<swear> sight."
msgstr ""
"Ok, ok. Voilà de l'eau et un peu de nourriture, <name_b>. Hors de ma <swear> "
"de vue."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Alright.  I gotta go."
msgstr "Ok. Je dois y aller."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Alright.  See ya."
msgstr "Ok. Au revoir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Care to talk for a bit?"
msgstr "Envie de discuter un peu?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Could I borrow something from the stock?"
msgstr "Je peux emprunter quelque chose du stock?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Could some money persuade you?"
msgstr "De l'argent pourrait vous persuader de changer d'avis?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Could you just chat for a bit?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid "Could you tell me a bit about yourself?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me raconter quelque chose à votre sujet?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Could you tell me about your hobbies again?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Do you have any hobbies?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Geez, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Ok. je m'en vais."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Has anyone stolen from here?"
msgstr "Quelqu'un a déjà volé d'ici?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"He was a nice fellow, taught me everything I know about firearms, wildlife, "
"and sailing.  We lived next to this big ol' lake, so we had plenty of "
"opportunities to catch bass and catfish.  He'd skin and filet them, and we'd "
"have it for dinner.  My mother always cooked them, and she was great at it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Hello.  What brings you around here?"
msgstr "Bonjour. Qu'est-ce qui vous amène?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "How much food do you have?"
msgstr "Quelle quantité de nourriture avez-vous?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I can give these people one less mouth to feed, if you'd prefer that."
msgstr ""
"Je peux faire en sorte qu'au moins les gens ici n'ait plus jamais besoin de "
"vous nourrir, si vous préférez."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I can understand that.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Je comprends. Parlons d'autre chose."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I don't know anymore, to tell you the truth.  I was planning on settling "
"down and having kids, but now that everyone's dead and the judgement of God "
"has come to pass, I'll seek His truth and try to keep on living.  One day, "
"when this is all over, I'll fly away to Heaven's pearly gates and be with "
"the angels.  As for the Earth, I'd rather not think about the things that "
"have come to pass."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I guess they will.  I pray to God that I won't have to shoot someone, I "
"never want to be forced into deciding between life or death."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I guess those shooting skills come in handy these days."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I have to go, see you later."
msgstr "Je dois y aller, à plus tard."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I hope it isn't too boring.  See ya."
msgstr "J'espère que ce ne sera pas trop ennuyant. Au revoir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I really like to draw things, I primarily did landscapes in my spare time.  "
"I like paper-and-pencil sketches, but I have worked with watercolors and oil "
"canvases.  Never could get my head around the digital stuff, though, too "
"complex for me and I never had a good free hand with a stylus.  I also shot "
"a bit, went hunting a few times.  I mainly went to the gun range though, "
"shotguns were always my forte.  Besides that, I watched some TV and regular "
"ol' stuff.  I also like to read quite a bit, too."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I used to work for the U.S Postal Service, I was a mail carrier.  Delivered "
"all the letters, packages, and mail orders to the residents of <city>, door-"
"to-door.  It was pretty hard at times, but it kept me fit and on the road."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I used to, me and my mother were pretty close.  I didn't know my father very "
"well for the first four years of my life, he was always out on deployment "
"with the Navy someplace.  Me and him got to know each other after he retired "
"from the service, we'd always go fishing on Sunday afternoons for years.  My "
"mother though, she was the sweetest lady you'd ever meet, always took care "
"of me and Dad.  Now they're gone, been that way for the last three years."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I won't.  Pleasure doin' business."
msgstr "Je ne piperai pas un mot. Un plaisir de faire affaire avec vous."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I'm alright at it, I guess.  I'm no Van Gough or Botticelli, but I get along "
"with it and do my best.  I've started using the desk up here to work on "
"these days, I just need to keep my firearm close and one eye on the door."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"I'm just a regular guy, been with the Church for a while now.  I kept a "
"good, solid job before <the_cataclysm>, lived in a nice apartment on "
"Chestnut Street."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Is that why you joined the Church?"
msgstr "Est-ce pour cela que vous avez rejoint l'Église?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help you?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelque chose que je puisse faire pour vous aider?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Just stopping by for a moment.  See ya."
msgstr "Je m'arrêtais juste pour un moment. Au revoir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Keep that in mind."
msgstr "Gardez-ça en tête."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Name's Eddie.  I'm making sure this stockpile is alright."
msgstr ""
"Le nom est Eddie. Je suis ici juste pour faire en sorte que ses réserves ne "
"soient pas dérangées."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Nobody's tried to yet.  It can get a little boring sometimes, standing "
"around and doing nothing."
msgstr ""
"Personne n'a essayé pour l'instant, c'est un peu ennuyant de temps en temps "
"de rester debout à ne rien faire."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Nope, it couldn't.  Don't try and <swear> bribe me again, you <swear> "
"<name_b>."
msgstr ""
"Non, ça ne changera pas mon avis. N'essayez plus jamais de me <swear> de "
"soudoyer, <swear> <name_b>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Nope, you can't do that.  I'd like to help you, but we've already got enough "
"mouths to feed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Okay, here's some food and water.  Don't tell anyone I gave you that."
msgstr ""
"Ok, voilà de l'eau et un peu de nourriture. Ne dites à personne que je vous "
"ai donné(e) ça."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"She sure was, helped me through some very hard times in my life.  I used to "
"be bullied in middle school, whenever I'd get beat up, she'd always help "
"clean me up and tell me I'd be alright.  She had this recipe for peach "
"casserole too, best one in the world.  It was hard for me when she passed, "
"but I found some solace right here in this Church.  We'd always been "
"religious, but this one just clicked for me, ya know?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I'd be willing to purchase some.  I'll have to work up the money with "
"Helena, but I'm sure we've got it.  I'd prefer canned, and preserved goods.  "
"How much are you talkin'?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Sure, what's happening?"
msgstr "Bien sûr, qu'est ce qu'il y a?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "That's private info, <name_g>."
msgstr "Ce sont des informations privées <name_g>."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "What are you planning on doing in the future?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "What did you do for a job before <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "What was your father like?"
msgstr "Comment était votre père?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Who are you again?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous déjà?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Would you be willing to buy any food?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, her death was hard on me.  I wound up goin' here one day, and I felt "
"something come over me, like I belonged here.  I haven't left since, and "
"I've been able to move on with them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "You must be a very good artist then.  Do you still have time to draw?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "You're mother must've been very nice."
msgstr "Votre mère doit avoir été très gentille."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "You're mother sounds very nice, what was she like?"
msgstr ""

